# Line endings are LF everywhere, including on Windows checkouts.
#
# The Windows CI image sets `core.autocrlf=true` globally, so without this every file arrives with
# `\r\n`. That is invisible to the compiler and to rustfmt, and it broke a test that reads the
# crate's own source: a search for "\n}\n" finds nothing when the file says "}\r\n". The test now
# normalises what it reads, and this stops the next one from having to know that.
#
# No effect on committed content — everything in here is already LF. It only fixes what a checkout
# hands to the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so never touched.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.wav binary
*.onnx binary
